+// Reference offsets for the ORIGINAL reverse-engineered vmstate layout
+// (Firecracker v1.12.0, 1 vCPU, x86_64). We no longer apply these as absolute
+// positions. Firecracker's versionize format contains variable-length sections
+// (MSR/CPUID vectors, per-device state), so sections shift *independently*
+// between builds and a single global offset cannot realign all of them (this is
+// the "sections shift independently" bug the CHANGELOG lists as unfixed).
+//
+// Instead we anchor two things by content and derive the rest:
+//   1. the IOAPIC block, via its MMIO base constant 0xFEC00000, and
+//   2. the vCPU register block, via the EFER + APIC-base-MSR adjacency.
+// Everything from LAPIC..XSAVE is one rigid kvm-vcpu struct, so once EFER is
+// located the rest follow at the fixed intra-block deltas below (which, unlike
+// the absolute positions, are stable across builds).
+#[allow(dead_code)] // kept for documentation; IOAPIC is found by constant search
